<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The floppy bot: mosfet's Bot body as the root SCXML session. It owns the
  bot lifecycle and processing turns; its abilities are invoked children
  (decision D6: invoke lifecycle replaces mosfet's attachment protocol).

    inactive -bot.activate-> live { activating -> active { unfocused,
      focused, processing, cancelling_processing } }
    live -bot.deactivate-> deactivating -> inactive
    live -bot.reboot (from cognition)-> live (re-entered: every ability is
      cancelled and invoked again)
    cancelling_processing -cancel timeout-> degraded (a final sink)

  Abilities: live holds <invoke id="cognition"> and <invoke
  id="communication"> (abilities/communication.scx, which holds the
  conversation and speaking); leaving live cancels every ability (SCXML
  6.4), which replaces mosfet's cleanup states. An ability is ready when it
  sends its first bot.ability.offers; the body is active when every
  expected ability is ready. A run-tagged activation timer
  (activation_timeout_ms), an error event, or an ability ending while
  activating fails the activation (bot.activating.failed) back to inactive;
  an ability ending while active degrades the bot.

  Communication: bot.ability.communication.input from outside, while
  active, goes to the communication, which admits it into its
  conversation; the conversation's product (bot.ability.conversation.output
  whose last message is inbound) comes back as a stimulus like bot.input.
  The communication says a routed bot.ability.communication.respond
  through speaking and answers bot.ability.speaking.output or
  bot.ability.communication.failed, which the body logs.

  Turns: bot.input or a conversation product in unfocused or focused
  starts a processing turn; <bot:stimulus> writes the event's stimulus
  envelope {event, data, source}. The body counts the turn, computes the
  turn's attention bias with <bot:attention> (focus, focus_candidates:
  mosfet's attention_bias_for_turn from device identity only), assembles the turn's choices (below), sends bot.ability.cognition.input
  {turn, stimulus, focus, focus_candidates, choices} to the cognition, and
  arms bot.processing.timed_out
  (processing_timeout_ms) for the turn. Replies count only when they come
  from the cognition for the current turn. A timeout sends
  bot.ability.cognition.cancel {turn} and waits in cancelling_processing,
  bounded by cancel_timeout_ms clamped to 100..5000 ms: the acknowledgement
  fails the turn (bot.processing.failed); no acknowledgement degrades the
  bot. Stimuli that arrive during a turn wait, as <bot:stimulus>
  envelopes, in the data model queue (in order) and start the next turns, one per return to unfocused or focused,
  before any later event.

  Choices (mosfet's per-turn dispatch inventory, assembled by decision
  namespace elements): on processing entry the body reads its own choices
  with <decision:choice location="body_choices" events="bot.focus_device
  bot.clear_focus"> (the transitions on active, offered only while offering
  is true: bot.focus_device when the turn has focus candidates,
  bot.clear_focus when a device is focused), <decision:pin> pins
  bot.focus_device's device to an enum of the turn's focus_candidates, and
  <decision:assemble> appends each ability's latest bot.ability.offers
  choices tagged with the ability's invoke id as target (the body's own
  carry no target). Every schema is compacted ($schema, title and examples
  dropped); when the choices are still over 32 KiB (phase 4 spike (b): a
  relayed list of 48264 B fails the whole invoke tree) every description is
  dropped too, and if they are still over the turn fails without reaching
  the cognition. The routing table routes maps each offered event to the
  targets offering it.

  Routing: a completed turn goes through routing, where <decision:route>
  places each selected event of the output, in order, and the body sends it
  to its receiver: an event the body offered
  to itself (#_internal), else the ability whose invoke id is the
  selection's target, or the only ability offering it when the selection
  names none (#_<id>). A selection the routing table cannot place (not
  offered this turn, or an unoffered target) is dropped with
  <log label="bot.route.dropped">, and so is a routed body event that no
  transition takes (bot.focus_device for a device outside the turn's
  candidates, bot.clear_focus with nothing focused). floppy.routed [floppy
  name], raised after the selections, ends routing once every routed body
  event has been taken (the internal queue is FIFO).

  Outputs: the root has no parent, so each event the body emits is written
  as <log label="EVENT" expr="JSON data">: bot.activated,
  bot.activating.failed, bot.deactivated, bot.processing.completed,
  bot.processing.failed, and bot.output (the turn's selected events, one
  record per completed turn), plus the communication's
  bot.ability.speaking.output and bot.ability.communication.failed;
  bot.choices logs each turn's assembled
  choices as event@target, bot.route each routed selection, and bot.focus
  each focus change.

  Contracts: the body's own events reference schemas/ by event:schema and
  are rechecked by cond; the abilities' events are described in
  abilities/schemas/ (a schema reference cannot leave this directory) and
  rechecked by cond here.

  Running: scx run with an env file and this document, as for the builder
  (bots/builder/README.md), then bot.activate and bot.input on standard
  input. The cognition's stages need TYPESAFE_API_KEY (intuition's decision
  service) and FLOPPY_BASE_URL and FLOPPY_API_KEY (reasoning's generate
  service, no default backend); without them a turn fails.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:bot="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/bot"
       xmlns:decision="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/decision"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="floppy" initial="inactive">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- Configuration. -->
    <data id="model" expr="'Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next'"/>
    <data id="activation_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
    <data id="processing_timeout_ms" expr="300000"/>
    <data id="cancel_timeout_ms" expr="5000"/>
    <!-- The configured devices (none until phase 6) and the live source id
         each one reports from. -->
    <data id="devices" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="device_source_refs" expr="({})"/>
    <!-- Lifecycle: each entry into live is one run; the abilities expected
         and the offers each has sent this run. -->
    <data id="live_run" expr="0"/>
    <data id="expected" expr="['cognition', 'communication']"/>
    <data id="offers" expr="({})"/>
    <!-- Turns. -->
    <data id="turn" expr="0"/>
    <data id="focused_device" expr="null"/>
    <data id="stimulus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus_candidates" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="queue" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="pending" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The turn's choices and routing table, and its selections. -->
    <data id="offering" expr="false"/>
    <data id="body_choices" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="choices" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="choice_names" expr="''"/>
    <data id="routes" expr="({})"/>
    <data id="choices_over" expr="false"/>
    <data id="choices_size" expr="0"/>
    <data id="selections" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="routing_selections" expr="false"/>
    <data id="routed_selections" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="route" expr="null"/>
    <data id="degraded_reason" expr="null"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script>
    function isObject(value) {
      return value !== null &amp;&amp; typeof value === 'object' &amp;&amp; !Array.isArray(value);
    }
    function isTurn(value) {
      return Number.isInteger(value) &amp;&amp; value &gt;= 1;
    }
    function isOptionalString(value) {
      return value === undefined || value === null || typeof value === 'string';
    }
    function isEmptyObject(data) {
      return isObject(data) &amp;&amp; Object.keys(data).length === 0;
    }
    // schemas/bot.activate.json
    function validActivate(data) {
      return isObject(data)
        &amp;&amp; Object.keys(data).every(function (k) { return k === 'model'; })
        &amp;&amp; (data.model === undefined || (typeof data.model === 'string' &amp;&amp; data.model.length &gt; 0));
    }
    // schemas/bot.input.json
    function validInput(data) {
      if (!isObject(data)) { return false; }
      if (data.target_device !== undefined &amp;&amp; data.target_device !== null
          &amp;&amp; !(typeof data.target_device === 'string' &amp;&amp; data.target_device.length &gt; 0)) { return false; }
      if (data.priority !== undefined
          &amp;&amp; !(Number.isInteger(data.priority) &amp;&amp; data.priority &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; data.priority &lt;= 10)) { return false; }
      var o = data.observation;
      if (o === undefined || o === null) { return true; }
      return isObject(o)
        &amp;&amp; Object.keys(o).every(function (k) { return ['event', 'data', 'id', 'source', 'target'].indexOf(k) &gt;= 0; })
        &amp;&amp; typeof o.event === 'string' &amp;&amp; o.event.length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; o.data !== undefined
        &amp;&amp; isOptionalString(o.id) &amp;&amp; isOptionalString(o.source) &amp;&amp; isOptionalString(o.target);
    }
    // schemas/bot.focus_device.json
    function validFocus(data) {
      return isObject(data) &amp;&amp; typeof data.device === 'string' &amp;&amp; data.device.length &gt; 0;
    }
    // schemas/bot.reboot.json
    function validReboot(data) {
      return isObject(data) &amp;&amp; ['cognition_child_teardown_failed', 'cognition_cancel_teardown_failed',
        'cognition_detach_rollback_failed', 'learning_child_teardown_failed',
        'learning_detach_rollback_failed'].indexOf(data.reason) &gt;= 0;
    }
    // schemas/bot.processing.timed_out.json, bot.processing.cancel.timed_out.json,
    // and the turn-correlated ability events.
    function forTurn(data) {
      return isObject(data) &amp;&amp; data.turn === turn;
    }
    // abilities/schemas/bot.ability.offers.json
    function validOffers(data) {
      return isObject(data) &amp;&amp; typeof data.ability === 'string' &amp;&amp; data.ability.length &gt; 0
        &amp;&amp; Array.isArray(data.choices)
        &amp;&amp; data.choices.every(function (c) { return isObject(c) &amp;&amp; typeof c.event === 'string' &amp;&amp; c.event.length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; c.schema !== undefined; });
    }
    // abilities/schemas/bot.ability.cognition.output.json
    function validOutput(data) {
      return forTurn(data) &amp;&amp; Array.isArray(data.output)
        &amp;&amp; data.output.every(function (s) { return isObject(s) &amp;&amp; typeof s.event === 'string' &amp;&amp; s.event.length &gt; 0; });
    }
    function fromCognition() {
      return _event.invokeid === 'cognition';
    }
    function fromCommunication() {
      return _event.invokeid === 'communication';
    }
    // abilities/schemas/bot.ability.communication.input.json (the
    // communication rechecks it in full).
    function validCommunicationInput(data) {
      return isObject(data) &amp;&amp; Array.isArray(data.source_ids) &amp;&amp; data.source_ids.length &gt; 0
        &amp;&amp; Array.isArray(data.target_ids) &amp;&amp; data.content !== undefined
        &amp;&amp; typeof data.content_type === 'string' &amp;&amp; data.content_type.length &gt; 0;
    }
    // abilities/schemas/bot.ability.conversation.output.json, from the
    // communication: a conversation product (its last message inbound).
    function conversationProduct() {
      var data = _event.data;
      return fromCommunication() &amp;&amp; isObject(data) &amp;&amp; Array.isArray(data.messages)
        &amp;&amp; data.messages.length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; isObject(data.messages[data.messages.length - 1])
        &amp;&amp; data.messages[data.messages.length - 1].direction === 'inbound';
    }
    function allReady() {
      return expected.every(function (id) { return offers[id] !== undefined; });
    }
    // A routed body event: taken only while routing a turn's selections.
    function routed() {
      return routing_selections &amp;&amp; _event.type === 'internal';
    }
  </script>

  <state id="inactive">
    <transition event="bot.activate" event:schema="schemas/bot.activate.json"
                cond="validActivate(_event.data)" target="live">
      <assign location="model" expr="_event.data.model === undefined ? model : _event.data.model"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.activate">
      <log label="bot.rejected" expr="'bot.activate does not satisfy schemas/bot.activate.json'"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <state id="live" initial="activating">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="live_run" expr="live_run + 1"/>
      <assign location="offers" expr="({})"/>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <assign location="queue" expr="[]"/>
    </onexit>
    <invoke id="cognition" type="scxml" src="../../abilities/cognition.scx">
      <param name="model" expr="model"/>
    </invoke>
    <invoke id="communication" type="scxml" src="../../abilities/communication.scx"/>

    <!-- Each ability's latest offers; the first of a run is its readiness. -->
    <transition event="bot.ability.offers" cond="expected.indexOf(_event.invokeid) &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; validOffers(_event.data) &amp;&amp; _event.data.ability === _event.invokeid">
      <assign location="offers[_event.invokeid]" expr="_event.data.choices"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.deactivate" event:schema="schemas/bot.deactivate.json"
                cond="isObject(_event.data)" target="deactivating"/>
    <!-- Only the cognition may ask for a reboot: re-enter live. -->
    <transition event="bot.reboot" event:schema="schemas/bot.reboot.json"
                cond="fromCognition() &amp;&amp; validReboot(_event.data)" target="live">
      <log label="bot.reboot" expr="JSON.stringify(_event.data)"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="bot.reboot">
      <log label="bot.rejected" expr="'bot.reboot is taken only from the cognition with a schemas/bot.reboot.json reason'"/>
    </transition>

    <state id="activating">
      <onentry>
        <send id="activation-timer" event="floppy.activating.timed_out" delayexpr="activation_timeout_ms + 'ms'">
          <param name="run" expr="live_run"/>
        </send>
      </onentry>
      <onexit>
        <cancel sendid="activation-timer"/>
      </onexit>
      <transition cond="allReady()" target="active">
        <log label="bot.activated" expr="JSON.stringify({})"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="floppy.activating.timed_out" cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; isObject(_event.data) &amp;&amp; _event.data.run === live_run" target="inactive">
        <log label="bot.diagnostic" expr="'the abilities ' + JSON.stringify(expected.filter(function (id) { return offers[id] === undefined; })) + ' were not ready within ' + activation_timeout_ms + ' ms'"/>
        <log label="bot.activating.failed" expr="JSON.stringify({})"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="error.*" target="inactive">
        <log label="bot.diagnostic" expr="_event.name + ' while activating' + (_event.invokeid ? ' (from ' + _event.invokeid + ')' : '')"/>
        <log label="bot.activating.failed" expr="JSON.stringify({})"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="done.invoke" target="inactive">
        <log label="bot.diagnostic" expr="'the ability ' + _event.invokeid + ' ended while activating'"/>
        <log label="bot.activating.failed" expr="JSON.stringify({})"/>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <state id="active" initial="unfocused">
      <!-- An ability that ends while the bot is active leaves it degraded. -->
      <transition event="done.invoke" cond="expected.indexOf(_event.invokeid) &gt;= 0" target="degraded">
        <assign location="degraded_reason" expr="'the ability ' + _event.invokeid + ' ended while active'"/>
      </transition>
      <!-- Communication input from outside goes to the communication, whose
           conversation answers with a product (a turn's stimulus, below). -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.communication.input"
                  cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; validCommunicationInput(_event.data)">
        <send event="bot.ability.communication.input" target="#_communication">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.communication.input" cond="!_event.invokeid">
        <log label="bot.rejected" expr="'bot.ability.communication.input does not satisfy abilities/schemas/bot.ability.communication.input.json'"/>
      </transition>
      <!-- What the communication said, and its failures. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.output" cond="fromCommunication() &amp;&amp; isObject(_event.data) &amp;&amp; typeof _event.data.text === 'string'">
        <log label="bot.ability.speaking.output" expr="JSON.stringify(_event.data)"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.communication.failed" cond="fromCommunication() &amp;&amp; isObject(_event.data) &amp;&amp; typeof _event.data.message === 'string'">
        <log label="bot.ability.communication.failed" expr="JSON.stringify(_event.data)"/>
      </transition>
      <!-- The body's own choices (mosfet: focus on active, clear only while
           a device is focused), offered on processing entry and taken only
           as routed selections of the turn. -->
      <transition event="bot.focus_device" event:schema="schemas/bot.focus_device.json"
                  cond="offering ? focus_candidates.length &gt; 0 : (routed() &amp;&amp; validFocus(_event.data) &amp;&amp; focus_candidates.indexOf(_event.data.device) &gt;= 0 &amp;&amp; devices.indexOf(_event.data.device) &gt;= 0)">
        <assign location="focused_device" expr="_event.data.device"/>
        <log label="bot.focus" expr="focused_device"/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.clear_focus" event:schema="schemas/bot.clear_focus.json"
                  cond="offering ? focused_device !== null : (routed() &amp;&amp; isObject(_event.data) &amp;&amp; focused_device !== null)">
        <assign location="focused_device" expr="null"/>
        <log label="bot.focus" expr="'none'"/>
      </transition>

      <state id="unfocused">
        <transition cond="queue.length &gt; 0" target="processing">
          <assign location="stimulus" expr="queue.shift()"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.input.json"
                    cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; validInput(_event.data)" target="processing">
          <bot:stimulus location="stimulus" event="_event.name" data="_event.data" source="_event.invokeid"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.output" cond="conversationProduct()" target="processing">
          <bot:stimulus location="stimulus" event="_event.name" data="_event.data" source="_event.invokeid"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <state id="focused">
        <transition cond="queue.length &gt; 0" target="processing">
          <assign location="stimulus" expr="queue.shift()"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.input.json"
                    cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; validInput(_event.data)" target="processing">
          <bot:stimulus location="stimulus" event="_event.name" data="_event.data" source="_event.invokeid"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.output" cond="conversationProduct()" target="processing">
          <bot:stimulus location="stimulus" event="_event.name" data="_event.data" source="_event.invokeid"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- One turn of the cognition. -->
      <state id="processing">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="turn" expr="turn + 1"/>
          <bot:attention location="focus_candidates" focuslocation="focus" stimulus="stimulus"
                         devices="devices" focus="focused_device" sources="device_source_refs"/>
          <assign location="offering" expr="true"/>
          <decision:choice location="body_choices" events="bot.focus_device bot.clear_focus"/>
          <assign location="offering" expr="false"/>
          <decision:pin location="body_choices" event="bot.focus_device" property="device" values="focus_candidates"/>
          <!-- bound: 32 KiB, the failure message below names it. -->
          <decision:assemble location="choices" routeslocation="routes" choices="body_choices" offers="offers"
                             bound="32768" overlocation="choices_over" sizelocation="choices_size"/>
          <decision:names location="choice_names" choices="choices"/>
          <log label="bot.choices" expr="choice_names"/>
          <if cond="!choices_over">
            <send event="bot.ability.cognition.input" target="#_cognition">
              <content expr="({turn: turn, stimulus: stimulus, focus: focus, focus_candidates: focus_candidates, choices: choices})"/>
            </send>
            <send id="processing-timer" event="bot.processing.timed_out" delayexpr="processing_timeout_ms + 'ms'">
              <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
            </send>
          </if>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="processing-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <!-- The choices do not fit: the turn fails before the cognition. -->
        <transition cond="choices_over" target="returning">
          <log label="bot.processing.failed" expr="JSON.stringify({message: 'the turn\'s choices are ' + choices_size + ' bytes, over 32768', turn: turn})"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.output" cond="fromCognition() &amp;&amp; validOutput(_event.data)" target="routing">
          <log label="bot.output" expr="JSON.stringify({turn: turn, output: _event.data.output})"/>
          <log label="bot.processing.completed" expr="JSON.stringify({output: _event.data.output, focus_candidates: focus_candidates, turn: turn})"/>
          <assign location="selections" expr="_event.data.output"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" cond="fromCognition() &amp;&amp; forTurn(_event.data)" target="returning">
          <log label="bot.processing.failed" expr="JSON.stringify({message: typeof _event.data.message === 'string' &amp;&amp; _event.data.message.length &gt; 0 ? _event.data.message : 'the cognition failed', turn: turn})"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.processing.timed_out" event:schema="schemas/bot.processing.timed_out.json"
                    cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; forTurn(_event.data)" target="cancelling_processing">
          <log label="bot.processing.timed_out" expr="JSON.stringify({turn: turn})"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.cognition.cancel" target="#_cognition">
            <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.input.json"
                    cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; validInput(_event.data)">
          <bot:stimulus location="pending" event="_event.name" data="_event.data" source="_event.invokeid"/>
          <assign location="queue" expr="queue.concat([pending])"/>
          <log label="bot.deferred" expr="String(queue.length)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.output" cond="conversationProduct()">
          <bot:stimulus location="pending" event="_event.name" data="_event.data" source="_event.invokeid"/>
          <assign location="queue" expr="queue.concat([pending])"/>
          <log label="bot.deferred" expr="String(queue.length)"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- The turn timed out: wait (bounded) for the cognition's
           acknowledgement of the cancel. -->
      <state id="cancelling_processing">
        <onentry>
          <send id="cancel-timer" event="bot.processing.cancel.timed_out"
                delayexpr="Math.min(5000, Math.max(100, cancel_timeout_ms)) + 'ms'">
            <param name="turn" expr="turn"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="cancel-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.cancelled bot.ability.processing.cancelled"
                    cond="fromCognition() &amp;&amp; forTurn(_event.data)" target="returning">
          <log label="bot.processing.failed" expr="JSON.stringify({message: 'the turn timed out after ' + processing_timeout_ms + ' ms and was cancelled', turn: turn})"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.processing.cancel.timed_out" event:schema="schemas/bot.processing.cancel.timed_out.json"
                    cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; forTurn(_event.data)" target="degraded">
          <log label="bot.processing.cancel.timed_out" expr="JSON.stringify({turn: turn})"/>
          <assign location="degraded_reason" expr="'turn ' + turn + ': the cognition did not acknowledge its cancel'"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.input" event:schema="schemas/bot.input.json"
                    cond="!_event.invokeid &amp;&amp; validInput(_event.data)">
          <bot:stimulus location="pending" event="_event.name" data="_event.data" source="_event.invokeid"/>
          <assign location="queue" expr="queue.concat([pending])"/>
          <log label="bot.deferred" expr="String(queue.length)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="bot.ability.conversation.output" cond="conversationProduct()">
          <bot:stimulus location="pending" event="_event.name" data="_event.data" source="_event.invokeid"/>
          <assign location="queue" expr="queue.concat([pending])"/>
          <log label="bot.deferred" expr="String(queue.length)"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- The completed turn's selections, each sent to its receiver; the
           routed body events are taken (by active's transitions) before
           floppy.routed. -->
      <state id="routing">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="routing_selections" expr="true"/>
          <decision:route location="routed_selections" selections="selections" routes="routes"/>
          <foreach array="routed_selections" item="route">
            <if cond="route.dropped !== undefined">
              <log label="bot.route.dropped" expr="route.dropped"/>
            <elseif cond="route.target === null"/>
              <log label="bot.route" expr="route.event + ' -&gt; bot'"/>
              <send eventexpr="route.event" target="#_internal">
                <content expr="route.data"/>
              </send>
            <else/>
              <log label="bot.route" expr="route.event + ' -&gt; ' + route.target"/>
              <send eventexpr="route.event" targetexpr="'#_' + route.target">
                <content expr="route.data"/>
              </send>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <raise event="floppy.routed"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <assign location="routing_selections" expr="false"/>
          <assign location="selections" expr="[]"/>
          <assign location="routed_selections" expr="[]"/>
        </onexit>
        <transition event="floppy.routed" target="returning"/>
      </state>

      <!-- Back to attention: focused when a device is focused. -->
      <state id="returning">
        <transition cond="focused_device !== null" target="focused"/>
        <transition target="unfocused"/>
      </state>

      <!-- A reply that belongs to no current turn is dropped. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.cognition.output bot.ability.failed bot.ability.cognition.cancelled bot.ability.processing.cancelled"
                  cond="fromCognition()">
        <log label="bot.stale" expr="_event.name + ' for turn ' + (isObject(_event.data) ? _event.data.turn : 'none') + ' (current ' + turn + ')'"/>
      </transition>
      <!-- A routed body event no transition above took. -->
      <transition event="*" cond="routed() &amp;&amp; _event.name !== 'floppy.routed'">
        <log label="bot.route.dropped" expr="_event.name + ' was not taken'"/>
      </transition>
    </state>
  </state>

  <!-- Leaving live cancelled every ability. -->
  <state id="deactivating">
    <transition target="inactive">
      <log label="bot.deactivated" expr="JSON.stringify({})"/>
    </transition>
  </state>

  <!-- A sink: the cognition did not acknowledge a cancel, or ended while
       active. The bot takes no more turns: degraded is a top-level final
       state, so the session ends with the reason as its result. -->
  <final id="degraded">
    <onentry>
      <log label="bot.degraded" expr="degraded_reason"/>
    </onentry>
    <donedata>
      <param name="reason" expr="degraded_reason"/>
    </donedata>
  </final>
</scxml>
